  "honest_limits": [
    "The E. coli calibration uses THIS repo's 600-window samples, not P2's exact fit windows, so it validates the implementation rather than reproducing their measurement identically.",
    "The spec names the degenerate VALUE but not the WIDTH it was observed at, and this corpus reaches that value at k=14 rather than k=12. Which width P2 used is unresolved and is the one thing that would change how the two curves line up.",
    "Zero exact duplicate elements in either cell, so density is not inflated by repeated sequences -- but near-duplicates (mutational series of a shared parent) were NOT measured, and they would raise the ratio without adding diversity.",
    "Single strand as given. Pooling both strands would raise the ratio and is not done here.",
    "This is a property of the generator's training folds only. Folds 9 and 10 were not read.",
    "A count-model occupancy statistic says nothing about what a NEURAL model could extract from the same corpus; it bounds the count-model class the question was posed about."
  ]
